# Quick-mode runs are disposable local checks, never evidence. They use one
# repetition at one payload size, which cannot resolve the enforcement signal.
*-quick-r*/
# A dirty-tree run cannot be reproduced from a commit, so it cannot be evidence
# no matter how clean its numbers look. Evidence mode refuses to start on a dirty
# tree, and this pattern is the second half of that rule.
*-dirty-*/
